{
 "_what": "Pythia-6.9b pretraining ladder: the sub-1000-step acquisition window OLMo's release schedule cannot see. A SEPARATE STUDY, never pooled with M05's OLMo population (registrar [5425](b)).",
 "_why_pythia": "Its early checkpoints are LOG-SPACED -- 0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512 -- so eleven rungs sit BELOW OLMo's first non-zero step. Allen AI's finest stage1 granularity is 1,000 steps (modal gap 1000 across 1,407 of 1,421 intervals), so no OLMo run can resolve this window.",
 "_limits": [
  "Per-rung ALIGNMENT contrasts are impossible: the 154 rungs are pretraining only.",
  "The family DOES have an alignment arm at the endpoint (lomahony/eleuther-pythia6.9b-hh-sft and -hh-dpo, already scored), so a base->aligned contrast exists AT step 143000 and nowhere else. Correcting my own [5424], which said no alignment arm at all.",
  "Different lab, tokenizer (50,277 vs OLMo's 100,278) and corpus: comparisons with OLMo are cross-ladder and must be labelled so."
 ],
